==Draft lottery==
{{further|NBA Draft Lottery}}
The first 14 picks in the draft belonged to teams that had missed the [[2008 NBA Playoffs|playoffs]]; the order was determined through a lottery. The lottery determined the three teams that would obtain the first three picks on the draft. The remaining first-round picks and the second-round picks were assigned to teams in reverse order of their win–loss record in the [[2007–08 NBA season|previous season]]. As it is commonplace in the event of identical win–loss records, the NBA performed a random drawing to break the ties on April 18, 2008.<ref name="draftorder">{{Cite web |date=April 18, 2008 |title=Ties Broken for NBA Draft 2008 Order of Selection |url=http://www.nba.com/clippers/news/08lottery_ties_080418.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121110214654/http://www.nba.com/clippers/news/08lottery_ties_080418.html |archive-date=November 10, 2012 |access-date=April 18, 2011 |website=NBA.com |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref>

The lottery was held on May 20, 2008, in [[Secaucus, New Jersey]].<ref name="draftorder" />  The [[Chicago Bulls]], who had the ninth-worst record, won the lottery with just a 1.7% chance to win. The [[Miami Heat]] and [[Minnesota Timberwolves]], with the worst and third-worst records, respectively, won the second and third picks.

Below were the chances for each team to get specific picks in the 2008 draft lottery, rounded to three decimal places:<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 20, 2008 |title=Results of the 2008 NBA Draft Lottery |url=http://www.nba.com/nba_news/draft_lottery_results_080520.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100913110915/http://www.nba.com/nba_news/draft_lottery_results_080520.html |archive-date=September 13, 2010 |access-date=April 18, 2011 |website=NBA.com |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=May 20, 2008 |title=2008 NBA Draft Lottery odds |url=http://www.nba.com/pacers/news/lottery_odds_2008.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200727195957/https://www.nba.com/pacers/news/lottery_odds_2008.html |archive-date=July 27, 2020 |access-date=April 18, 2011 |website=NBA.com |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref>
