==Trades involving draft picks==

===Draft-day trades===
The following trades involving drafted players were made on the day of the draft.
*{{note label|Note1|a|a 1}}{{note label|Note1|a|2}} [[Memphis Grizzlies|Memphis]] acquired the draft rights to 3rd pick [[O. J. Mayo]], along with [[Marko Jarić]], [[Antoine Walker]], and [[Greg Buckner]], from [[Minnesota Timberwolves|Minnesota]] in exchange for the draft rights to 5th pick [[Kevin Love (basketball)|Kevin Love]], along with [[Mike Miller (basketball, born 1980)|Mike Miller]], [[Brian Cardinal]], and [[Jason Collins]].<ref name="draft day trade">{{Cite web |last=Schuhmann |first=John |date=June 26, 2008 |title=The Deals of the Draft |url=http://www.nba.com/draft2008/trades_20080626.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090312073840/http://www.nba.com/draft2008/trades_20080626.html |archive-date=March 12, 2009 |access-date=March 29, 2009 |website=NBA.com |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=June 26, 2008 |title=Wolves Acquire Love, Miller from Memphis |url=http://www.nba.com/timberwolves/news/wolves_acquire_love_miller_from_memphis_080626.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090524072327/http://www.nba.com/timberwolves/news/wolves_acquire_love_miller_from_memphis_080626.html |archive-date=May 24, 2009 |access-date=April 23, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Timberwolves |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref>
*{{note label|Note2|b|b 1}}{{note label|Note2|b|2}} [[Portland Trail Blazers|Portland]] acquired the draft rights to 11th pick [[Jerryd Bayless]] and [[Ike Diogu]] from [[Indiana Pacers|Indiana]] in exchange for the draft rights to 13th pick [[Brandon Rush]], [[Jarrett Jack]] and [[Josh McRoberts]].<ref name="draft day trade" /> The trade was finalized on July 9, 2008.<ref name="pacers trade">{{Cite web |date=July 9, 2009 |title=Pacers Announce Two Trades; Acquire Seven Players |url=http://www.nba.com/pacers/news/pacers_trades_release_080709.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120825195712/http://www.nba.com/pacers/news/pacers_trades_release_080709.html |archive-date=August 25, 2012 |access-date=April 23, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Pacers |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref>
*{{note label|Note3|c|c 1}}{{note label|Note3|c|2}} [[Toronto Raptors|Toronto]] acquired [[Jermaine O'Neal]] and the draft rights to 41st pick [[Nathan Jawai]] from [[Indiana Pacers|Indiana]] in exchange for [[T. J. Ford]], [[Rasho Nesterovič]], [[Maceo Baston]], and the draft rights to 17th pick [[Roy Hibbert]].<ref name="draft day trade" /> The trade was finalized on July 9, 2008.<ref name="pacers trade" />
*{{note label|Note4|d|d 1}}{{note label|Note4|d|2}}{{note label|Note4|d|3}}{{note label|Note4|d|4}} In a three-team trade, Portland acquired the draft rights to 25th pick [[Nicolas Batum]] from [[Houston Rockets|Houston]], Houston acquired the draft rights to 33rd pick [[Joey Dorsey]] from Portland and the draft rights to 28th pick [[Donté Greene]] and a 2009 second-round draft pick from Memphis, and Memphis acquired the draft rights to 27th pick [[Darrell Arthur]] from Portland.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note5|e|e}}Portland acquired the draft rights to 27th pick [[Darrell Arthur]] from [[New Orleans Hornets|New Orleans]] in exchange for cash considerations.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note6|f|f 1}}{{note label|Note6|f|2}}{{note label|Note6|f|3}} [[Detroit Pistons|Detroit]] acquired the draft rights to 32nd pick [[Walter Sharpe]] and 46th pick [[Trent Plaisted]] from Seattle in exchange for the draft rights to 29th pick [[D. J. White]].<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note7|g|g}} [[Miami Heat|Miami]] acquired the draft rights to 34th pick [[Mario Chalmers]] from Minnesota in exchange for two future second-round draft picks and cash considerations.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note8|h|h 1}}{{note label|Note8|h|2}} In a three-team trade, [[Chicago Bulls|Chicago]] acquired the draft rights to 36th pick [[Ömer Aşık]] from Portland, the Trail Blazers acquired a second-round draft pick in 2009 from Denver and two future second-round draft picks from Chicago, and Denver acquired the draft rights to 39th pick [[Sonny Weems]] from Chicago.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note9|i|i 1}}{{note label|Note9|i|2}} [[San Antonio Spurs|San Antonio]] acquired the draft rights to 48th pick [[Malik Hairston]], a second-round draft pick in 2009, and cash considerations from Phoenix in exchange for the draft rights to 45th pick [[Goran Dragić]].<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note10|j|j}} Boston acquired the draft rights to 47th pick [[Bill Walker (basketball)|Bill Walker]] from [[Washington Wizards|Washington]] in exchange for cash considerations.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note11|k|k}} Cleveland acquired the draft rights to 52nd pick [[Darnell Jackson]] from [[Miami Heat|Miami]] in exchange for 2009 second-round draft pick.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note12|l|l}}The [[Los Angeles Clippers|L.A. Clippers]] acquired the draft rights to 55th pick [[Mike Taylor (basketball player)|Mike Taylor]] from Portland in exchange for a 2009 second-round draft pick.<ref name="draft day trade" />
*{{note label|Note13|m|m}} Cleveland acquired the draft rights to 56th pick [[Sasha Kaun]] from Seattle in exchange for cash considerations.<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 26, 2008 |title=Cavaliers Acquire Draft Rights to Darnell Jackson and Sasha Kaun |url=http://www.nba.com/cavaliers/news/arthur_kaun_080626.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090313235050/http://www.nba.com/cavaliers/news/arthur_kaun_080626.html |archive-date=March 13, 2009 |access-date=March 29, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Cavaliers |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref>

