*{{note label|Note27|aa|aa}} On February 23, 2006, Seattle acquired a 2008 second-round draft pick, [[Earl Watson]] and [[Bryon Russell]] from [[Denver Nuggets|Denver]] in a four-team trade.<ref>{{Cite web |date=January 23, 2006 |title=Sonics Acquire Russell and Watson in Four-Team Deal |url=http://www.nba.com/sonics/news/russellwatson060223.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080708144219/http://www.nba.com/sonics/news/russellwatson060223.html |archive-date=July 8, 2008 |access-date=March 29, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Thunder |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref> Seattle used the pick to draft [[DeVon Hardin]].
*{{note label|Note28|ab|ab}} On June 7, 2007, Miami acquired 2007 and 2008 second-round draft picks from [[Orlando Magic|Orlando]] as part of the hiring of [[Stan Van Gundy]] as Orlando's head coach.<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 8, 2007 |title=Magic close book on Donovan by hiring Van Gundy |url=https://www.espn.com/nba/news/story?id=2895929 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090213072505/http://sports.espn.go.com/nba/news/story?id=2895929 |archive-date=February 13, 2009 |access-date=March 29, 2009 |website=ESPN.com}}</ref> Miami used the pick to draft [[Darnell Jackson]].
*{{note label|Note29|ac|ac}} On February 21, 2008, Houston re-acquired their 2008 second-round draft pick along with [[Bobby Jackson (basketball)|Bobby Jackson]] and [[Adam Haluska]] from New Orleans in a three-team trade.<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 21, 2008 |title=Hornets Acquire Wells and James from Rockets |url=http://www.nba.com/hornets/news/HORNETS_ACQUIRE_WELLS_AND_JAME-258879-31.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201120130519/http://www.nba.com/hornets/news/HORNETS_ACQUIRE_WELLS_AND_JAME-258879-31.html |archive-date=November 20, 2020 |access-date=April 30, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Hornets |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref> Previously, Houston and New Orleans agreed to exchange second-round draft picks in a trade that sent [[Kirk Snyder]] to Houston on July 14, 2006.<ref name="Kirk Snyder trade">{{Cite web |date=July 14, 2006 |title=Hornets Trade Kirk Snyder To Houston |url=http://www.nba.com/hornets/news/Hornets_Trade_Snyder_13Jul2006.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100114212111/http://www.nba.com/hornets/news/Hornets_Trade_Snyder_13Jul2006.html |archive-date=January 14, 2010 |access-date=April 10, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Hornets |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref> Houston used the pick to draft [[Maarty Leunen]].
*{{note label|Note30|ad|ad}} On June 28, 2006, Portland acquired Indiana's 2007 and Phoenix's 2008 second-round draft picks and the draft rights to [[Alexander Johnson (basketball)|Alexander Johnson]] from Indiana in exchange for the draft rights to [[James White (basketball)|James White]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 28, 2006 |title=Trail Blazers Land Brandon Roy and LaMarcus Aldridge |url=http://www.nba.com/blazers/news/Trail_Blazers_Land_Brandon_Roy-183312-1177.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071228041019/http://www.nba.com/blazers/news/Trail_Blazers_Land_Brandon_Roy-183312-1177.html |archive-date=December 28, 2007 |access-date=April 30, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Blazers |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref> Previously, Indiana acquired a 2008 second-round draft pick on August 25, 2005, from Phoenix in exchange for [[James Jones (basketball, born 1980)|James Jones]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 25, 2005 |title=Phoenix Acquires James Jones from Indiana |url=http://www.nba.com/suns/news/james_050825.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090116044713/http://www.nba.com/suns/news/james_050825.html |archive-date=January 16, 2009 |access-date=March 29, 2009 |website=NBA.com/Suns |publisher=Turner Sports Interactive, Inc}}</ref> Portland used the pick to draft [[Mike Taylor (basketball player)|Mike Taylor]].
*{{note label|Note31|ae|ae}} On June 28, 2007, Seattle acquired New Orleans' 2008 second-round draft pick and cash considerations from Houston in exchange for the draft rights to [[Carl Landry]].<ref name="sonics2007" /> Previously, Houston and New Orleans agreed to exchange second-round draft picks in a trade that sent Kirk Snyder to Houston on July 14, 2006.<ref name="Kirk Snyder trade" /> Seattle used the pick to draft [[Sasha Kaun]].

